class SlytherScript
class SlytherArtifact {
    Represents an instantiated artifact defined in an #{SlytherScript}, contains:

    - artifact: The kind of the artifact, ex. class, function, etc...
    - name: The name of the artifact to be created, optionally qualified as `Parent::child` to declare it
      inside another artifact; the parent must be declared too, otherwise it must throw an error
    - content: The prose written inside the artifact
    - references: `kind:name` of the references found in the artifact prose, defined as \#{Reference}, escaped as \\#{Reference}, if the symbol is not found, it must throw an error
    - hash: The hash of the artifact, the name and the content
}

class SlytherClosureHasher {
    Computes the closure hash of every #{SlytherArtifact} of a list, keyed by `kind:name`.

    The closure hash of an artifact covers its own hash and, transitively, the hash of everything it
    references, so it changes whenever any artifact it depends on changes. A `Parent::child` name is a
    dependency of its parent as well, so a parent changes whenever one of its children changes.

    It is cycle tolerant: mutually referencing artifacts are hashed as a single group, and each member
    of the group mixes its own hash into the group's, so members of a cycle keep distinct closure hashes.
}

class ParsedSlytherScript {
    Represents a parsed SlytherScript, contains:

    - artifacts: A list of #{SlytherArtifact} that were parsed from the #{SlytherScript}
    - closureHashes: The closure hash of every artifact, keyed by `kind:name`, as computed by #{SlytherClosureHasher}
}

class SlytherParser {
    Reads a #{SlytherScript} and returns a #{ParsedSlytherScript}
}
